=== D.4 POWER: WHAT EFFECT WAS DETECTABLE? ===

The thesis concludes there are no two-way interactions between the focal
variables. With the Model 2 samples we can compute the minimum detectable
effect (MDE) at 80% power and alpha 0.05: MDE = (t_crit + t_pow) * SE.

    model          term estimate    se p_value  mde mde_sd
   M2_rep x_rep:x_brand    0.166 0.467   0.723 1.31  0.766
   M2_rep   x_rep:x_pop   -0.371 0.461   0.422 1.29  0.755
   M2_pop x_pop:x_brand    0.392 0.546   0.475 1.53  0.976
   M2_pop   x_pop:x_rep   -0.744 0.539   0.170 1.51  0.963
 M2_brand x_brand:x_rep    0.251 0.507   0.621 1.42  0.895
 M2_brand x_brand:x_pop   -0.677 0.511   0.188 1.43  0.902

Reading: the design could only detect interactions on the order of
1.29-1.53 Likert points (0.75-0.98 standard deviations). Absence of
evidence is not evidence of absence: these results are inconclusive, not null.


